      "writtenOn": "2021-04-21T16:14:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need an entry for ec-s5 as well.  Seems like an oversight that cros-ec doesn\u0027t include an entry for SENSOR_CONFIG_EC_S5.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "508e81576d3f2c3083edb1803f1e4ba490276a41",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d2f2b15_e267613d",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/trogdor/lazor/motionsense.dts",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-21T19:39:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked around and it seems that only 2 boards actually set that config. It seems to be used for gesture detection, are we sure we want it?",
      "parentUuid": "987ab1f3_e450b722",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "508e81576d3f2c3083edb1803f1e4ba490276a41",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7461ca8e_80a0d14a",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/trogdor/lazor/motionsense.dts",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-22T15:24:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the history, Lazor enables the sensors in S5 so that the board init code can detect which sensor is installed during initialization and before the the AP is powered up. See CQ:2606166\n\nSo this is okay as it matches cros-ec.   My open concern is what does motionsense do with an uninitialized odr value?  If setting the odr to zero stops scanning, that is desired behavior, as we really just need the sensor powered on.\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/793c8e2f/common/motion_sense.c#158",
      "parentUuid": "8d2f2b15_e267613d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "508e81576d3f2c3083edb1803f1e4ba490276a41",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75c9553c_0d5726ea",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/trogdor/lazor/motionsense.dts",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-22T17:15:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The config array is set to have a length of SENSOR_CONFIG_MAX so we don\u0027t overflow, so it is then initialized to an odr of 0 (https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/motion_sense.h;l\u003d209;drc\u003d90995b4a525442b448384e8c5e6d77f541283c4d). So it\u0027s the same as setting:\n\nec-s5 {\n  odr \u003d \u003c0\u003e;\n};\n\nWhich I think is what you\u0027re saying that you want?",
      "parentUuid": "7461ca8e_80a0d14a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "508e81576d3f2c3083edb1803f1e4ba490276a41",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd57124c_7cc8ec1a",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/trogdor/lazor/motionsense.dts",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-21T16:14:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Related to http://issuetracker.google.com/183990188#comment4, the Lazor board supports the ICM426xx IMU as a second source sensor.  We will need to compile in the ICM426xx driver and then add the board_detect_motionsensor() to make a runtime decision as to the active sensor.\n\nCan you add the framework to compile in the ICM426xx driver?  Once b:183990188 solves the runtime update of motion_sensors[], we can do something similar with the I2C probing.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "508e81576d3f2c3083edb1803f1e4ba490276a41",
